WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:01.980
- [Instructor] In this video,

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.260
we're going to get a little
bit of practice multiplying

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.690
and dividing decimals

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.930
by 10, 100, and 1000.

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.720
So let's just start with
a little bit of a warmup.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.720
If I were to say, what is 2.05 times 10?

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.110
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:21.650
Well, in previous videos,

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.170
we've already said that
when you multiply by 10,

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.470
you shift each of the digits
one place to the left.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.610
And so this is going to be equal to,

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.690
instead of two ones,

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.870
we're now going to have two 10s,

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.580
so two in the tens place.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.580
And then, instead of zero tenths,

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.563
we're now going to have zero ones.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.170
And instead of five hundredths,

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.490
we're now going to have five tenths,

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.620
so this is equal to 20.5.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.650
Now what if we were to
go the other way around?

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.910
What if we were to say 2.05

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.390
divided by 10?

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.073
Pause the video and see if
you can figure that out.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.430
Well here,

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.280
all of our digits are going to
shift one place to the right

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.710
because we're dividing by 10.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.720
You could also view that
as multiplying by 1/10.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.970
And so our two ones are
going to become two tenths,

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.540
so this is going to be zero point,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.610
so we're gonna have two tenths now.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.220
Our zero tenths are
going be zero hundredths,

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:20.910
and then our five hundredths

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.200
are going to be five thousandths,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.220
we've covered that in other videos,

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:29.470
but now let's do this
with, say, 100 or 1000.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.870
So if I were to ask you

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:36.340
what is 57

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.240
divided by 1000?

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.680
Pause this video and see
if you can work that out.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.580
All right, now let's do this together.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.550
So when you divide by 1000,

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.660
that's the same thing as
dividing by 10 three times.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.340
Or it's the same thing as multiplying

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.730
by 1/10 three times,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.020
or you could just say hey,

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.720
that means I'm going to shift each

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.390
of these digits three places to the right,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.520
and so let me create some places here.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.810
So that's 10s, ones,

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.150
tenths, hundredths, thousandths,

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:17.150
and so our five was in the
10s place, it's five 10s,

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.020
so it was here,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.488
but we're going to shift
three places to the right.

00:02:22.488 --> 00:02:24.613
One, two, three.

00:02:24.613 --> 00:02:26.388
So our five will go there.

00:02:26.388 --> 00:02:30.655
So what was five 10s
is now five hundredths.

00:02:30.655 --> 00:02:34.752
And then our seven is similarly going to,

00:02:34.752 --> 00:02:36.732
it was in the ones place,

00:02:36.732 --> 00:02:39.261
but we're gonna shift
three places to the right.

00:02:39.261 --> 00:02:41.140
One, two, three.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.420
And there you have it.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.840
What was just 57 is now 57 thousandths.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.040
And to make that very clear,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.720
I'll put a zero in the tenths place

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.970
and a zero in the ones place,

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.350
and that makes sense.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:54.620
So as another example,

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.850
let's say someone walks
up to you on the street

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.040
and says I started with 1.032

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.300
and I multiplied it by something

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.813
and I was able to get 103.2.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.150
What did they multiply by to get 103.2?

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.150
Pause this video and try to work it out.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.530
Well to understand this,

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.363
we just have to think well,

00:03:22.363 --> 00:03:24.630
how much did each digit

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:25.980
get shifted by?

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.310
So what was in the ones
place got shifted not just

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.810
to the 10s place, but it got
shifted to the hundreds place.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:37.700
So it got shifted two places to the left.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.530
The zero, similarly, got
shifted two places to the left.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.760
From the tenths to the 10s,

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:44.630
and if you look at it,

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:47.430
every digit got shifted
two places to the left.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:50.490
And we must have multiplied by 10 twice,

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.970
so you could say times 10 times 10,

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:57.410
or you could just rewrite
this as times 100.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:00.970
Let's just do one more example for kicks.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.530
Let's say that someone were to say

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:09.530
what is 0.015 times 100?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.350
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.550
All right, well, like we've done before,

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.620
we're just going to shift every digit

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.330
two places to the left.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:26.130
So the one, which is in
the hundredths place,

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.770
is going to end up in the ones place,

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:32.750
and then the five, which is
in the thousandths place,

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.530
is going to end up in the tenths place.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:38.640
So this is going to be equal to 1.5,

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.633
and we're done.

